 The SKIP entry remains truthful and unaltered: on this system, MinGW’s gcc terminates with exit code 1, producing no output, for a program whose `main` returns zero, whereas the identical C loader source builds and succeeds under MSVC in the immediately following section. The harness reports which of those two outcomes occurred, instead of labeling a defective compiler as a fault in the source.
 
